{"name":"Pretty Lady","hex":"#c3a1b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pretty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pleasant to the sight or other senses; attractive, especially of women or children. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of objects or things: nice-looking, appealing."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Somewhat, fairly, quite; sometimes also (by meiosis) very.","Prettily, in a pretty manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty"},{"term":"lady","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The mistress of a household.","A woman of breeding or higher class, a woman of authority."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To address as “lady”."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lady"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pretty Lady (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Pretty Lady is an album by pianist Les McCann recorded in 1961 and released on the Pacific Jazz label."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fd/Pretty_Lady_%28album%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretty_Lady_(album)","wikidata":"Q25095513"},{"title":"Pretty Lady (Keith Stegall song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pretty Lady\" is a song written and recorded by American country music artist Keith Stegall. It was released in May 1985 as the fourth single from his self-titled debut album. The song peaked at number 10 on the Billboard Hot Country Singles chart. It also reached number 12 on the RPM Country Tracks chart in Canada."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretty_Lady_(Keith_Stegall_song)","wikidata":"Q7242240"},{"title":"Pretty Lady (Lighthouse song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pretty Lady\" is a 1973 song by Canadian rock band Lighthouse. The song was the lead single of three released from their Can You Feel It LP. \nIt was written by lead singer Skip Prokop."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/e/e3/Pretty_Lad